Description: A workflow based on 'scTenifoldNet' to perform in-silico knockout 
    experiments using single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data from wild-type 
    (WT) control samples as input. First, the package constructs a single-cell 
    gene regulatory network (scGRN) and knocks out a target gene from the 
    adjacency matrix of the WT scGRN by setting the gene's outdegree edges to 
    zero. Then, it compares the knocked out scGRN with the WT scGRN to identify 
    differentially regulated genes, called virtual-knockout perturbed genes, 
    which are used to assess the impact of the gene knockout and reveal the 
    gene's function in the analyzed cells. This version includes C++ acceleration 
    with Eigen library, cross-platform compatibility (macOS, Linux, Windows), 
    and Seurat v4/v5 support.
